msgid ""
msgstr ""
"# Installation and Environment Configuration\n"
"\n"
"## 1. Environment Preparation\n"
"\n"
"Before installing Triton-Ascend, ensure the following environment dependencies are met:\n"
"\n"
"- **Operating System**: Ubuntu 20.04 or later (64-bit), or openEuler 22.03 LTS\n"
"- **Python**: 3.8–3.11 (64-bit)\n"
"- **Ascend NPU driver and firmware**: Version 23.0.rc1 or later\n"
"- **CANN Toolkit**: Version 6.2 or later\n"
"- **PyTorch**: Version 1.11 or later (optional, required only for the PyTorch extension)\n"
"- **torch_npu**: Version matching the CANNN version (optional, required only for the PyTorch extension)\n"
"\n"
"> **Note**: The Ascend NPU driver, firmware, and CANN Toolkit must be installed and configured before installing Triton-Ascend. For installation instructions, see the [CANN Installation Guide](https://www.hiascend.com/document).\n"
"\n"
"## 2. Installing Triton-Ascend\n"
"\n"
"### 2.1 Installing from Source\n"
"\n"
"1. Clone the Triton-Ascend repository:\n"
"\n"
"   ```bash\n"
"   git clone https://github.com/Ascend/Triton-Ascend.git\n"
"   cd Triton-Ascend\n"
"   ```\n"
"\n"
"2. Create and activate a Python virtual environment (recommended):\n"
"\n"
"   ```bash\n"
"   python3 -m venv triton-ascend-env\n"
"   source triton-ascend-env/bin/activate\n"
"   ```\n"
"\n"
"3. Install the dependencies:\n"
"\n"
"   ```bash\n"
"   pip install -r requirements.txt\n"
"   ```\n"
"\n"
"4. Build and install Triton-Ascend:\n"
"\n"
"   ```bash\n"
"   python setup.py install\n"
"   ```\n"
"\n"
"### 2.2 Installing via pip\n"
"\n"
"You can also install Triton-Ascend directly using pip:\n"
"\n"
"```bash\n"
"pip install triton-ascend\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"> **Note**: The pip package may not include the latest features and bug fixes. For the latest version, install from source.\n"
"\n"
"## 3. Environment Configuration\n"
"\n"
"After installation, configure the following environment variables:\n"
"\n"
"| Environment Variable | Description | Default Value |\n"
"| -------------------- | ----------- | ------------- |\n"
"| `ASCEND_HOME` | Ascend NPU installation path | `/usr/local/Ascend` |\n"
"| `ASCEND_TOOLKIT_HOME` | CANN Toolkit installation path | `$ASCEND_HOME/ascend-toolkit/latest` |\n"
"| `LD_LIBRARY_PATH` | Path to the Ascend NPU shared libraries | `$ASCEND_TOOLKIT_HOME/lib64` |\n"
"| `PYTHONPATH` | Path to the Ascend NPU Python modules | `$ASCEND_TOOLKIT_HOME/python/site-packages` |\n"
"\n"
"Add the following lines to your shell configuration file (e.g., `~/.bashrc`):\n"
"\n"
"```bash\n"
"export ASCEND_HOME=/usr/local/Ascend\n"
"export ASCEND_TOOLKIT_HOME=$ASCEND_HOME/ascend-toolkit/latest\n"
"export LD_LIBRARY_PATH=$ASCEND_TOOLKIT_HOME/lib64:$LD_LIBRARY_PATH\n"
"export PYTHONPATH=$ASCEND_TOOLKIT_HOME/python/site-packages:$PYTHONPATH\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"Then, reload the configuration:\n"
"\n"
"```bash\n"
"source ~/.bashrc\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"## 4. Verifying the Installation\n"
"\n"
"To verify that Triton-Ascend is installed correctly, run the following Python script:\n"
"\n"
"```python\n"
"import triton\n"
"import triton_ascend\n"
"\n"
"print(f\"Triton version: {triton.__version__}\")\n"
"print(f\"Triton-Ascend version: {triton_ascend.__version__}\")\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"If the installation is successful, the output should be similar to the following:\n"
"\n"
"```\n"
"Triton version: 3.0.0\n"
"Triton-Ascend version: 0.1.0\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"## 5. Troubleshooting\n"
"\n"
"### 5.1 `ImportError: No module named 'triton_ascend'`\n"
"\n"
"This error indicates that Triton-Ascend is not installed or the Python environment is incorrect. Check the following:\n"
"\n"
"- Ensure that Triton-Ascend is installed in the current Python environment.\n"
"- Ensure that the virtual environment is activated (if used).\n"
"- Check the `PYTHONPATH` environment variable.\n"
"\n"
"### 5.2 `RuntimeError: Ascend NPU is not available`\n"
"\n"
"This error indicates that the Ascend NPU driver or CANN Toolkit is not installed or configured correctly. Check the following:\n"
"\n"
"- Ensure that the Ascend NPU driver and firmware are installed and the NPU is visible (`npu-smi info`).\n"
"- Ensure that the CANN Toolkit is installed and the environment variables are set correctly.\n"
"- Ensure that the current user has permission to access the NPU device.\n"
"\n"
"### 5.3 Compilation errors\n"
"\n"
"If you encounter compilation errors during installation, ensure that the build dependencies are installed:\n"
"\n"
"```bash\n"
"pip install cmake ninja\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"If the problem persists, collect the error logs and submit an issue on the [Triton-Ascend GitHub repository](https://github.com/Ascend/Triton-Ascend/issues).\n"

msgid "安装指南"
msgstr "Installation Guide"

msgid "**Triton-Ascend**是适配华为Ascend处理器的Triton优化版本，主要用于提供高效的核函数自动调优、算子编译及部署能力，支持Ascend Atlas A2/A3/950系列产品，兼容Triton核心语法的同时，针对昇腾NPU特性进行了深度优化，包括自动解析核函数参数、优化内存访问逻辑、完善安全部署机制等,在昇腾平台上快速开发和部署高性能计算任务。"
msgstr "**Triton-Ascend** is an optimized version of Triton adapted for Huawei Ascend processors, primarily designed to provide efficient kernel autotuning, operator compilation, and deployment capabilities. It supports Ascend Atlas A2/A3/950 series products and, while remaining compatible with core Triton syntax, has been deeply optimized for Ascend NPU features, including automatic parsing of kernel parameters, optimization of memory access logic, and enhancement of secure deployment mechanisms, enabling rapid development and deployment of high-performance computing tasks on the Ascend Platform."

